<div class="eyebrow">NATHAN AI 🚀 · ONE · ORIGINALS FIRST · ADD, DO NOT REPLACE</div><h1>The Vatican Master Recovery</h1><p>Papal history, scripture comparisons, the Vatican → England → America audit, 312-network positions, secret passages, books, games, ciphers and engines. Your original materials remain intact in the owner-controlled recovery ZIP; this public browser has a separate research index.</p>
<section><h2>Recovered reference coverage</h2><div id="stats" class="stats"></div><p><small>All 100 network slots are displayed, but their original row wording has not been recovered. The requested 101-event historical audit has only 69 recovered positions.</small></p></section>
<section><h2>Search the connected collections</h2><div class="controls"><div><label for="group">Collection</label><select id="group"><option value="all">All source-indexed records</option><option value="documents">72 historical document references</option><option value="audit">Historical audit 1–69</option><option value="network">312 Network positions 213–312</option><option value="subjects">Vatican investigation subjects</option><option value="works">Books, games, ciphers, engines</option><option value="author-words">Author declarations</option><option value="private-files">Original file inventory</option></select></div><div><label for="search">Search by subject, word, year or title</label><input id="search" type="search" placeholder="Unam Sanctam, 1213, Jesuits, VAULT" autocomplete="off"></div><button id="export" type="button">Export public index JSON</button></div><p id="results-status" role="status"></p><div id="cards" class="grid"></div><button id="more" type="button" hidden>Show 40 more results</button></section>
<section><h2>Evidence and recovery boundaries</h2><div id="corrections"></div><details><summary>Missing and unverified materials</summary><ul id="gaps"></ul></details><p><strong>Historical-audit headings are not legal findings.</strong> Source documents, author claims, accusations, and literary/game concepts remain separately labeled.</p></section>
<section><h2>Bring every original file in privately</h2><p>Your full preservation package contains <strong>13 source files</strong>, the recovery index, and a file manifest. Those original bytes are not made public through GitHub. Open the existing <a href="../../../vault.html">ONE Owner Vault</a> and import the recovery ZIP on your own device. The text selector below is a temporary preview only and does not upload any content.</p><label for="private">Select original .txt, .md, or .json file(s) from your device</label><input id="private" type="file" accept=".txt,.md,.json,text/plain,application/json" multiple><button id="clear" type="button">Clear private preview</button><p id="private-status" role="status">No private files selected.</p><div id="private-preview"></div><p><small>Selected files remain in this browser session only; they are excluded from the public catalog export. Images and ZIP files can be imported to the separate owner vault.</small></p></section>
<footer>1+1=2 BUILD · 1−1=0 CLEAR · Source → Index → Evidence → Compare → Story/Game · No third-party account access or background synchronization.</footer>
